+EMS SaaS Industrial 6.4.1 — Strict Targeted Hardening
+
+Base: cb15919032596021e732321a4c7c84e60429f5f6
+
+Key changes:
+- Fix PostgreSQL startup crash caused by parameter binding in ALTER TABLE ... SET DEFAULT.
+- Preserve STATE_VERSION=4 compatibility with safe defaults for newly introduced state fields.
+- Harden local command recovery and strict lifecycle handling.
+- Do not allow direct QUEUED -> EXECUTING transitions.
+- Persist EXECUTING state before any GPIO mutation; abort hardware mutation when durable state persistence fails.
+- Use a 120-second delivery lease and 300-second absolute command expiry.
+- Keep terminal completion separate from ACKED confirmation.
+- Prevent reassignment of RETIRED Pi devices.
+- Keep feedback_enabled consistent with device-level feedback hardware capability.
+- Use explicit EMS_DATA_DEVICE provisioning and a least-privilege systemd service.
+- Keep protected GPIO/storage/resource subsystems unchanged from the baseline.
+
+Not certified by this ZIP:
+HIL/electrical qualification, endurance/wear qualification, Alembic migration qualification, secure OTA/rollback, browser/session security finalization, dependency vulnerability closure, and full production CI/deployment qualification.
